# Script Safety

All PowerShell scripts in `scripts/` must:

- Be Windows PowerShell friendly (5.1+ compatible). Do not use heredocs.
- Use `Set-StrictMode -Version Latest` and `$ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"`.
- Validate input paths before acting; fail clearly with helpful messages.
- Be non-destructive by default. Require an explicit `-Force` to overwrite existing files.
- Never write secrets, tokens, keys, or connection strings to disk or logs.
- For export, always run `scan_before_export.ps1` first and abort if it fails.
- Use an explicit allowlist/exclusion model when copying to client repos; never assume content is safe.
- Print a clear summary of what was created, copied, or excluded.
- Return non-zero exit codes on failure so CI and chained scripts can stop.
